{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21ea7e39d99b57bc5a9c", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Work, Power and Energy - Test 1", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 50, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0ae7"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0aa1", "title": "Physics Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a04", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e96"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e3c"], "question": {"text": "A porter lifts a heavy suitcase of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>80</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> and at the destination lowers it down by a distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>80</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> with a constant velocity. Calculate the work done by the porter in lowering the suitcase. (take&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ms</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> )"}, "options": [{"id": "cae840", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>62720</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a05"}, {"id": "31434f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>627</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a06"}, {"id": "c0b831", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>627</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a07"}, {"id": "5b7237", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>784</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a08"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a09", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476b"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4721"], "question": {"text": "Which one of the following forces cannot be expressed in terms of potential energy?"}, "options": [{"id": "80003c", "text": "Coulomb's force", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a0a"}, {"id": "232fa8", "text": "Gravitational force", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a0b"}, {"id": "e09de2", "text": "Frictional force", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a0c"}, {"id": "c37179", "text": "Restoring force", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a0d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a0e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b68"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b2b"], "question": {"text": "A particle moves in $x-y$ plane under the influence of a force $\\vec{F}$ such that its linear momentum is $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{p}}(\\mathrm{t})=\\hat{i} \\cos (\\mathrm{kt})-\\hat{j} \\sin (\\mathrm{kt})$. If $\\mathrm{k}$ is constant, the angle between $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{F}}$ and $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{p}}$ will be :"}, "options": [{"id": "f5c6bb", "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{4}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a0f"}, {"id": "2893c2", "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{6}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a10"}, {"id": "daf98f", "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a11"}, {"id": "85b19b", "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{3}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a12"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a13", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["6117b9b867dbe2603c3ea8cc"], "concepts": ["6117b9d167dbe2603c3eaca6"], "question": {"text": "A stone tide to a string of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> is whirled in a vertical circle with the other end of the string at the centre. At a certain instant of time, the stone is at its lowest position and has a speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>u</mi></math>. The magnitude of change in its velocity, as it reaches a position where the string is horizontal, is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfenced></msqrt></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is"}, "options": [{"id": "81fbff", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a14"}, {"id": "429ba5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a15"}, {"id": "ec2d27", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a16"}, {"id": "9bfe1d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a17"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a18", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e96"], "concepts": ["60e567aa499d1e49588f95c3"], "question": {"text": "Consider a force <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover></math> . The work done by this force in moving a particle from point <math><mi>A</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1,0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> to <math><mi>B</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0,1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> along the line segment is : (all quantities are in SI units)<p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F37e2ddc8-042c-4a98-8294-be89e21fd9a3-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 195px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "9663d5", "text": "<math><mn>2</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a19"}, {"id": "ef0924", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a1a"}, {"id": "42833e", "text": "<math><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a1b"}, {"id": "da6546", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a1c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a1d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476b"], "concepts": ["6117b8bd67dbe2603c3e85b3"], "question": {"text": "<p>A small particle of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> moves in such a way that its potential energy&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#969;</mi></math>&nbsp;is constant and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math> is the distance of the particle from origin. Assuming Bohr&rsquo;s quantization of momentum and circular orbit, the radius of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi>th</mi></msup></math> orbit will be proportional to</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "223b12", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a1e"}, {"id": "307402", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a1f"}, {"id": "58f209", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a20"}, {"id": "5a93fe", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a21"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a22", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b68"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87c4"], "question": {"text": "A constant power delivering machine has towed a box, which was initially at rest, along a horizontal straight line. The distance moved by the box in time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math> is proportional to :-"}, "options": [{"id": "536285", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>t</mi><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a23"}, {"id": "d58a08", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>t</mi><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a24"}, {"id": "2bbd89", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a25"}, {"id": "96a2f7", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>t</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a26"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a27", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["6117b9b867dbe2603c3ea8cc"], "concepts": ["6117b9d167dbe2603c3eaca6"], "question": {"text": "A body of mass ' \\(m\\) ' connected to a massless and unstretchable string goes in verticle circle of radius ' \\(R\\) 'under gravity \\(g\\). The other end of the string is fixed at the center of circle. If velocity at top of circular path is \\(n \\sqrt{g R}\\), where, \\(n \\geqslant 1\\), then ratio of kinetic energy of the body at bottom to that at top of the circle is"}, "options": [{"id": "ac6bcd", "text": "\\(\\frac{n^2}{n^2+4}\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a28"}, {"id": "595c64", "text": "\\(\\frac{n^2+4}{n^2}\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a29"}, {"id": "2cf270", "text": "\\(\\frac{n+4}{n}\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a2a"}, {"id": "f2dc3b", "text": "\\(\\frac{n}{n+4}\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a2b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a2c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e96"], "concepts": ["617aa9bdef3fe65ad8e80f6d"], "question": {"text": "A uniform cable of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> and length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> is placed on a horizontal surface such that its <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></mrow></msup></math> part is hanging below the edge of the surface. To lift the hanging part of the cable upto the surface, the work done should be:"}, "options": [{"id": "1e871f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a2d"}, {"id": "6fa6eb", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a2e"}, {"id": "af47c6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a2f"}, {"id": "b908a6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>M</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a30"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a31", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476b"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f00"], "question": {"text": "A body is released from a height equal to the radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>R</mi></mfenced></math> of the earth. The velocity of the body when it strikes the surface of the earth will be: (Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo></math> acceleration due to gravity on the earth.)"}, "options": [{"id": "921c5b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a32"}, {"id": "590add", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a33"}, {"id": "2a48f9", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>4</mn><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a34"}, {"id": "ccda46", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a35"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a36", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b68"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e3f"], "question": {"text": "Sand is being dropped from a stationary dropper at a rate of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> on a conveyor belt moving with a velocity of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The power needed to keep belt moving with the same velocity will be"}, "options": [{"id": "6b8bf7", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a37"}, {"id": "c39385", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a38"}, {"id": "830f14", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a39"}, {"id": "444d87", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a3a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a3b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["6117b9b867dbe2603c3ea8cc"], "concepts": ["6117b9d167dbe2603c3eaca6"], "question": {"text": "A ball suspended by a thread swings in a vertical plane so that its magnitude of acceleration in the extreme position and lowest position are equal. The angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi><mo>)</mo></math> of thread deflection in the extreme position will be :"}, "options": [{"id": "974227", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>)</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a3c"}, {"id": "8b4a1b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a3d"}, {"id": "9ff0aa", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a3e"}, {"id": "8c57a3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a3f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a40", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e96"], "concepts": ["6162fadf6ed13040ec8486fd"], "question": {"text": "A person pushes a box on a rough horizontal plateform surface. He applies a force of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>N</mi></math> over a distance of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi></math>. Thereafter, he gets progressively tired and his applied force reduces linearly with distance to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>N</mi></math>. The total distance through which the box has been moved is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi></math>. What is the work done by the person during the total movement of the box?"}, "options": [{"id": "bda77f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3280</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a41"}, {"id": "bfc8c0", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2780</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a42"}, {"id": "610553", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5690</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a43"}, {"id": "aa4e04", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5250</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575d