elationship is true?"}, "options": [{"id": "71bc08", "text": "$\\mathrm{P} \\propto \\sqrt{v}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a4b"}, {"id": "ee7c42", "text": "$\\mathrm{P} \\propto v$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a4c"}, {"id": "34de8a", "text": "$\\mathrm{P}^2 \\propto v^5$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a4d"}, {"id": "dfe408", "text": "$\\mathrm{P}^2 \\propto v^3$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a4e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a4f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["6117b9b867dbe2603c3ea8cc"], "concepts": ["6117b9d167dbe2603c3eaca6"], "question": {"text": "For a particle in uniform circular motion, the acceleration <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> at any point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> on the circular path of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is (when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi></math> is measured from the positive <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math> is uniform speed):"}, "options": [{"id": "04fb3a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a50"}, {"id": "dbddb7", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</m