mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>, the incorrect statement for this system is :</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Ff7dd0df4-adcb-4dcd-81ed-0b0628b65d9b-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 284px; height: 242px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "ac67fe", "text": "at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></math>. is constant throughout the region.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a55"}, {"id": "fbe063", "text": "at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></math>. is smallest and the particle is moving at the slowest speed.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a56"}, {"id": "5ae55a", "text": "at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></math>. is greatest and the particle is moving at the fastest speed.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a57"}, {"id": "9fb871", "text": "at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a58"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a59", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e96"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e3c"], "question": {"text": "A block of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kg</mi></math> slides over a distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> on a horizontal surface. If the co-efficient of friction between the surfaces is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></math> , then the work done against friction (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>) is:"}, "options": [{"id": "658f92", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4200</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a5a"}, {"id": "049f4d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3900</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a5b"}, {"id": "31d0b5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4000</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a5c"}, {"id": "114dec", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4500</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a5d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a5e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b68"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e3f"], "question": {"text": "In a reactor,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>&nbsp;of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><none></none><mn>235</mn><mprescripts></mprescripts><mn>92</mn><none></none></mmultiscripts></math>&nbsp;fuel is fully used up in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn></math>&nbsp;days. The energy released fission is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>MeV</mi></math>. Given that the Avogadro number,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>023</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>26</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;per kilo mole and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>eV</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>19</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>. The power output of the reactor is close to:"}, "options": [{"id": "39e470", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>35</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>MW</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a5f"}, {"id": "6df62b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>MW</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a60"}, {"id": "5fc6e6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>125</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>MW</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a61"}, {"id": "0f6b30", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>54</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>MW</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a62"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a63", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["6117b9b867dbe2603c3ea8cc"], "concepts": ["6117b9d167dbe2603c3eaca6"], "question": {"text": "A body of mass 100 g is moving in circular path of radius 2 m on vertical plane as shown in figure. The velocity of the body at point $A$ is $10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$. The ratio of its kinetic energies at point $B$ and $C$ is :\n\n\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Ff9RYC1ZHxMpG7ENS5r2i3ZU3ATQpdPt4-CasDS7h3mM.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>\n\n\n(Take acceleration due to gravity as $10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}^2$ )"}, "options": [{"id": "6bf8d8", "text": "$\\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{3}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a64"}, {"id": "9a8908", "text": "$\\frac{2+\\sqrt{3}}{3}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a65"}, {"id": "959767", "text": "$\\frac{3+\\sqrt{3}}{2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a66"}, {"id": "bb445e", "text": "$\\frac{3-\\sqrt{2}}{2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0a67"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283e223cf4b3ad8f125e6", "title": "JEE Single Correct", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:15.785Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:43.682Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:43.682Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0ae5"}, {"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0ae3", "title": "Physics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0ac7", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e96"], "concepts": ["60e567aa499d1e49588f95c3"], "question": {"text": "A force $\\left(3 x^2+2 x-5\\right) \\mathrm{N}$ displaces a body from $x=2 \\mathrm{~m}$ to $x=4 \\mathrm{~m}$. Work done by this force is ________ $J$."}, "options": [{"id": "2aa7f4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0ac8"}, {"id": "c318f4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0ac9"}, {"id": "74f975", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0aca"}, {"id": "c365fe", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0acb"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0acc", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476b"], "concepts": ["6117b8bd67dbe2603c3e85b3"], "question": {"text": "<p>An object of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;initially at rest on a smooth horizontal plane starts moving under the action of force <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>. In the process of its linear motion, the angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi></math> (as shown in figure) between the direction of force and horizontal varies as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math> is a constant and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is the distance covered by the object from its initial position. The expression of kinetic energy of the object will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">k</mi></mfrac><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;is ______.</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F01b39f2a-6cbf-4008-af64-51e019c28c14-9894258.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 157px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "db7532", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0acd"}, {"id": "8c7d5f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0ace"}, {"id": "f2b107", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0acf"}, {"id": "684102", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0ad0"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0ad1", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b68"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e3f"], "question": {"text": "A body of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> is driven by an engine delivering a constant power of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. the body starts from rest and moves in a straight line. After <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>,&nbsp;the body has moved a distance (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>)&hellip;."}, "options": [{"id": "9ac21b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0ad2"}, {"id": "dc4bee", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0ad3"}, {"id": "eded4d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0ad4"}, {"id": "5ffbbc", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0ad5"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0ad6", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["6117b9b867dbe2603c3ea8cc"], "concepts": ["6117b9d167dbe2603c3eaca6"], "question": {"text": "A small bob tied at one end of a thin string of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> is describing a vertical circle so that the maximum and minimum tension in the string is in the ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. The velocity of the bob at the highest position is&nbsp;______&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. (Take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>)"}, "options": [{"id": "e9a7dc", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0ad7"}, {"id": "a3400e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0ad8"}, {"id": "17d577", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0ad9"}, {"id": "f23755", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0ada"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0adb", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e96"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e3c"], "question": {"text": "A force $\\mathrm{f}=\\mathrm{x}^2 \\mathrm{y} \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}+\\mathrm{y}^2 \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}$ acts on a particle in a plane $\\mathrm{x}+\\mathrm{y}=10$. The work done by this force during a displacement from $(0,0)$ to $(4 \\mathrm{~m}, 2 \\mathrm{~m})$ is $\\qquad$ Joule (round off to the nearest integer)"}, "options": [{"id": "83dd67", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0adc"}, {"id": "206c5f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0add"}, {"id": "a26505", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0ade"}, {"id": "7756b0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f575dcf815cd79e0adf"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8f125e5", "title": "JEE Numerical", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:27.056Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c